## Recommended Batch 17 — pick ONE primary direction:

### Direction A — E-commerce Phase 3-heavy (Xendit checkout, T3 batch, ~50-70K)
The remaining major E-commerce gap. Requires Architect-Execute split (§4 memory-governance.md)
since a single Opus session would hit context pressure. Recommended task decomposition:
- Item 0 (Opus, ~5K): Add `xendit-node` to apps/web/package.json + `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile=false`.
  Create `apps/web/src/lib/xendit.ts` thin client wrapper reading XENDIT_SECRET_KEY from env.
- Item 1 (Sonnet ~20K): `storefront.createXenditInvoice` protected writeProcedure — input
  orderId; verify order is pending, create Xendit invoice, persist invoiceId to
  `EcommerceOrder.xenditPaymentId`, return invoice_url for redirect. Tests for happy path +
  duplicate-invoice-rejection + invalid order status.
- Item 2 (Sonnet ~25K): Webhook handler at `apps/web/src/app/api/webhooks/xendit/route.ts` —
  x-callback-token verification (constant-time compare per security.md), idempotency via
  `xenditPaymentId` lookup, update `paymentStatus` from webhook event type, return 200 even
  on duplicate (idempotency contract). Tests for token mismatch (401), missing token (401),
  invalid payload (400), duplicate webhook (200 idempotent), happy path (200 + DB updated).
- Item 3 (Opus ~10K): "Pay with Xendit" Client Component button on order detail page that
  calls createXenditInvoice mutation + window.location to returned invoice_url.

### Direction B — Storefront cart + checkout flow (no payment yet, T2-T3, ~30-50K)
Layer cart state on top of public storefront before adding payment. Two items:
- Item 1 (T2): Cart Client Component with localStorage persistence on product detail page
  "Add to cart" button. Cart drawer triggered from store layout. No tRPC yet — pure client state.
- Item 2 (T2): Checkout page `/store/checkout` Server Component shell + Client Component form
  reading cart from localStorage, posting to `storefront.placeOrder` (already shipped in Batch 14).
  Customer self-resolution via session OR guest checkout via emailed login.

### Direction C — Mobile WatermelonDB DTR Phase 1a (Expo scaffold only, T2-T3, ~40-60K)
Pre-work for Direction B mobile. Single batch goal: minimal Expo app that boots, has nav
+ auth + theme + connects to existing tRPC. WatermelonDB defers to Phase 1b in Batch 18+.
- Item 1: `apps/mobile/` Expo scaffold + app.json + tsconfig + minimal Login screen calling
  `/api/trpc/auth.signIn`. Drawer/tab nav stub. Theme matching shadcn/ui dark variant.

### Direction D — Small carry-forward bundle (Tier 1-2, ~15-25K combined, SAFE)
- Item 1: Wrap `accounting.reverse` in `db.$transaction` + 3-4 partial-failure rollback tests.
  Branch: `fix/batch-17-item-1-accounting-reverse-tx`. Pre-flight: confirm procedure name +
  path — grep returned no match in Batch 16 pre-flight, so re-verify in apps/web/src/server/trpc/routers/accounting.ts.
- Item 2: Add `AUTH_TRUST_HOST=true` to `.env.staging`, `.env.prod`, `scripts/sync-credentials-to-env.sh`.
  Branch: `chore/batch-17-item-2-auth-trust-host`. Pre-flight: confirmed missing in Batch 16.
- Item 3 (optional): Quotation builder Phase 3 column reorder + named template save/load.
  T2 ~15-20K solo. Branch: `feat/batch-17-item-3-quotation-column-templates`.

## New recurring-pattern lessons surfaced during Batch 16 (apply at Batch 17 PRE-FLIGHT):

- Partial-update Zod procedure pattern works cleanly: conditional spread in `.data` only
  writes fields the client explicitly set. Pair with Client Component dirty tracking that
  only sends changed fields. Applies to any "small admin edit form on existing record"
  (e.g. Direction D Item 3 quotation column templates if picked).

- Nested-relation Prisma filter when no back-relation anchor: `where: { products: { some: { ... } } }`
  is cleaner than fetching all parents + filtering client-side. Avoids N+1 count queries.
  Also `where: { category: { slug: input } }` skips a slug→id→categoryId roundtrip.

- Pre-flight item 9 (public-route × procedure-auth) is a KEEPER. Paid off again in Batch 16
  with zero execution pivots. Make it permanent in pre-flight going forward.

- 656 tests in 20 files still run in <3s total. No need to scope to single-file vitest during
  item development — full-suite regression after each item is fast and catches cross-router
  fallout (none this batch, but cheap insurance).

- Path drift hazard: .whatsnext occasionally references stale paths (e.g.
  `apps/web/src/server/routers/` instead of `apps/web/src/server/trpc/routers/`). Always
  verify path exists via `ls` or `find` before quoting in pre-flight grep commands.

